{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>And the men of the place asked about his wife.</b> The reason Rivka was not taken immediately, as Sarah was taken, is because Avraham had already rebuked them, as we said earlier in the section of וירא, where he said to them: a guest who came to the city, etc." "<b>Lest he kill me.</b> But Avraham was not afraid, at the end of the matter, to say 'she is my wife,' because they feared him on account of the war against Amrafel and his companions, whom he defeated. But they did not fear Yitzchak; therefore Yitzchak was afraid." "<b>For she is fair of appearance.</b> And it is not written מאד (very), because she had given birth. But before she gave birth, in the section of חיי (the life of Sarah), מאד is written of her."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:06:03.468650882Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}